WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.725
Every control that blocks an admin path
also creates a way to lock yourself out.

2
00:00:04.725 --> 00:00:10.113
So there's one standing exception:
emergency access, or break-glass, accounts.

3
00:00:10.113 --> 00:00:15.598
Two cloud-only accounts, permanently Global
Administrator, with phishing-resistant

4
00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:19.306
sign-in of their own, excluded
only from blocking policies,

5
00:00:19.306 --> 00:00:20.851
and alerted on every use.

6
00:00:20.851 --> 00:00:24.725
Using them is strict: two
senior administrators together,

7
00:00:24.725 --> 00:00:29.246
only when PIM is down and the problem
can't wait, out within four hours,

8
00:00:29.246 --> 00:00:32.637
reviewed within a day, and
tested every ninety days.

9
00:00:32.637 --> 00:00:33.863
Two decisions.

10
00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:36.962
Build and test them before
any role goes eligible.

11
00:00:36.962 --> 00:00:39.317
And be honest in the security plan:

12
00:00:39.317 --> 00:00:44.449
NIST expects emergency accounts to
expire, so record these as a deviation.

13
00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:48.025
The CISO builds; the
authorizing official accepts.

14
00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:49.460
Now, who decides.
